(354064, 27559, 7485, '<td valign="top">Very interesting perspctive and good DOF+ lighting. With so much symmetry, I would have continued it all the way down and either included both heels or neither.</td>', 'Very interesting perspctive and good DOF+ lighting. With so much symmetry, I would have continued it all the way down and either included both heels or neither.', '2003-07-11 18:41:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(354065, 28077, 6388, '<td valign="top">the model may be nude, but the photo is blurry, and the colour is odd (not just the toes - the feet look off-hue as well).  If your camera struggles with close-ups, try using lots of light and even a magnifying glass ( an inexpensive alternative to a macro lens).</td>', 'the model may be nude, but the photo is blurry, and the colour is odd (not just the toes - the feet look off-hue as well).  If your camera struggles with close-ups, try using lots of light and even a magnifying glass ( an inexpensive alternative to a macro lens).', '2003-07-11 18:42:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(354067, 28223, 4543, '<td valign="top">Nice tatoo.  Great Lightning. 6.</td>', 'Nice tatoo.  Great Lightning. 6.', '2003-07-11 18:43:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(354068, 28229, 7485, '<td valign="top">Now that''s interesting lighting! But it would have been a much more powerful photo as a true nude, without the  swimtrunks (with the water ripples, it could still have been PG).</td>', 'Now that''s interesting lighting! But it would have been a much more powerful photo as a true nude, without the  swimtrunks (with the water ripples, it could still have been PG).', '2003-07-11 18:44:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(354069, 28058, 6388, '<td valign="top">your backlight is  alittle bright I think - exposure is a little hot on the right, which causes the shadows to eat a bit too much of the form on the left.  Did you do some editing along her back?  the texture of the backdrop looks off (my guess is dodging some shadows?).  Great idea, and nice composition.</td>', 'your backlight is  alittle bright I think - exposure is a little hot on the right, which causes the shadows to eat a bit too much of the form on the left.  Did you do some editing along her back?  the texture of the backdrop looks off (my guess is dodging some shadows?).  Great idea, and nice composition.', '2003-07-11 18:44:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(354073, 28286, 6388, '<td valign="top">exposure seems a little hot on the backdrop, and a little cold on the figure''s back.  bringing the lightmore from the back, and a little less from the right side would even it out a little.  Interesting composition - different.</td>', 'exposure seems a little hot on the backdrop, and a little cold on the figure''s back.  bringing the lightmore from the back, and a little less from the right side would even it out a little.  Interesting composition - different.', '2003-07-11 18:46:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(354075, 28298, 6388, '<td valign="top">I think the crop may be a little tight...I have to really look to get an appreciation for what i''m looking at.  lighting is nice, tones are rich, focus is sharp. overall solid image.</td>', 'I think the crop may be a little tight...I have to really look to get an appreciation for what i''m looking at.  lighting is nice, tones are rich, focus is sharp. overall solid image.', '2003-07-11 18:47:57.000000', NULL, 1),
