(354106, 28283, 7485, '<td valign="top">Great pose and very good use of a simple editing trick. But the grey halo around all the black areas (compression artifact?) is a bit distracting.</td>', 'Great pose and very good use of a simple editing trick. But the grey halo around all the black areas (compression artifact?) is a bit distracting.', '2003-07-11 19:05:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(354107, 28222, 6388, '<td valign="top">I like it.  nice pose, nice toning (I''m referring to the shades of grey, but HER toning is nice too :) ), great subject.  something is bothering me about the shadow on her elbow...the lighting is unnatural, and though I can''t figure out why, i''m going to hazard a guess it''s post-shot editing. Did you blur the background after the fact, or do some dodging?    Overall very nice effect - one of my favourites of the challenge.</td>', 'I like it.  nice pose, nice toning (I''m referring to the shades of grey, but HER toning is nice too :) ), great subject.  something is bothering me about the shadow on her elbow...the lighting is unnatural, and though I can''t figure out why, i''m going to hazard a guess it''s post-shot editing. Did you blur the background after the fact, or do some dodging?    Overall very nice effect - one of my favourites of the challenge.', '2003-07-11 19:06:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(354108, 28271, 6388, '<td valign="top">as i said of the other shots in the challenge like this:  the composition is quite obvious (kind of like saying "here''s my boob" in a documentary fashion).  using alittle more negative space onthe right would ease the composition a bit...it almost leads you off the page, rather than into the photo.  <br/>don''t love the red hue, and I can''t tell if that''s lighting of post-shot. either way it''s takes away some of the necessary detail for me.</td>', 'as i said of the other shots in the challenge like this:  the composition is quite obvious (kind of like saying "here''s my boob" in a documentary fashion).  using alittle more negative space onthe right would ease the composition a bit...it almost leads you off the page, rather than into the photo.  don''t love the red hue, and I can''t tell if that''s lighting of post-shot. either way it''s takes away some of the necessary detail for me.', '2003-07-11 19:09:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(354109, 28078, 7485, '<td valign="top">One of the best ones here. Excellent use of high contrast and both saturated and desaturated (or dynamic range somehow quantized) color, and the intimate pose really tells a story.</td>', 'One of the best ones here. Excellent use of high contrast and both saturated and desaturated (or dynamic range somehow quantized) color, and the intimate pose really tells a story.', '2003-07-11 19:10:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(354110, 28282, 6388, '<td valign="top">creative shot - really like the angle and depth (also the judicious use of water stream :) ).  few hot spots (like on your chin) which could easily be edited out by dropping the contrast, or (in this challenge) burning them out.</td>', 'creative shot - really like the angle and depth (also the judicious use of water stream :) ).  few hot spots (like on your chin) which could easily be edited out by dropping the contrast, or (in this challenge) burning them out.', '2003-07-11 19:11:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(354113, 27979, 6388, '<td valign="top">a little soft in the focus.  toning is nice, but the lighting is off.  Try using a reflector to lose some of the shadows, or move the model away form the curtain with a longer lens.  Compositionally, it doesn''t grab me as more than a person handcuffed in boots standing in front of a curtain.  It has potential to be more, but somehow just didn''t grab me.  good effort, either way.</td>', 'a little soft in the focus.  toning is nice, but the lighting is off.  Try using a reflector to lose some of the shadows, or move the model away form the curtain with a longer lens.  Compositionally, it doesn''t grab me as more than a person handcuffed in boots standing in front of a curtain.  It has potential to be more, but somehow just didn''t grab me.  good effort, either way.', '2003-07-11 19:13:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(354114, 27336, 7485, '<td valign="top">Love the effect on the water surface! Now if you\''d just skipped the banana and given us a little more of the model...</td>', 'Love the effect on the water surface! Now if you\''d just skipped the banana and given us a little more of the model...', '2003-07-11 19:15:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(354115, 28116, 6388, '<td valign="top">too much light breaks through yonder window.  the exposure is too ht over there, and distracts from what is some outstanding hair.  A diffused fill-flash would work (even through a piece of paper) I''d have liked to see this one cropped a little lower, to catch a little low-back and the ends of her hair.</td>', 'too much light breaks through yonder window.  the exposure is too ht over there, and distracts from what is some outstanding hair.  A diffused fill-flash would work (even through a piece of paper) I''d have liked to see this one cropped a little lower, to catch a little low-back and the ends of her hair.', '2003-07-11 19:16:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(354117, 27336, 6388, '<td valign="top">I assume that''s a post-processing edit filter (shrink wrap?), but it doesn''t add to the image to me.  I like the setup (maybe without the banana) and the colour is good too.  I should make a melon joke here, but I won''t.  I''m above that.  :)</td>', 'I assume that''s a post-processing edit filter (shrink wrap?), but it doesn''t add to the image to me.  I like the setup (maybe without the banana) and the colour is good too.  I should make a melon joke here, but I won''t.  I''m above that.  :)', '2003-07-11 19:18:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(354118, 27589, 6388, '<td valign="top">Filters giveth, and filters taketh away.  this one takes away form the image, as does the border.  compositionally, I like it, and i think the lighting is good (buit the filter makes it hard to tell)  Good on ya for taking a chance, ,but this time it didn''t work.</td>', 'Filters giveth, and filters taketh away.  this one takes away form the image, as does the border.  compositionally, I like it, and i think the lighting is good (buit the filter makes it hard to tell)  Good on ya for taking a chance, ,but this time it didn''t work.', '2003-07-11 19:20:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(354120, 28191, 6388, '<td valign="top">done with a projector, or post shot edit?  interesting effect anyway...contemplated one like this myself.  good effort.</td>', 'done with a projector, or post shot edit?  interesting effect anyway...contemplated one like this myself.  good effort.', '2003-07-11 19:21:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(354123, 27897, 6388, '<td valign="top">i doubt you''ll get a lot of high marks on this, since the effect is very non-photographic.  I do this kind of thing to photos a lot, but I don''t consider them photos after that :)  Aside from the edits, i like the composition - breaks a way from the fairly predictable profile shot (4 or 5 in this challenge alone).  can''t tell you what i think about the lighting, since the edit removes it''s effect.</td>', 'i doubt you''ll get a lot of high marks on this, since the effect is very non-photographic.  I do this kind of thing to photos a lot, but I don''t consider them photos after that :)  Aside from the edits, i like the composition - breaks a way from the fairly predictable profile shot (4 or 5 in this challenge alone).  can''t tell you what i think about the lighting, since the edit removes it''s effect.', '2003-07-11 19:24:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(354126, 27571, 6388, '<td valign="top">lighting is good, use of space is good, crop is good, subject (while attractive) leaves something to be desired.  it''s a little unnatural I guess ("hmm. there''s a maid.  and there''s her boob".)  They''re good boobs, don''t get me wrong, but I think you could have done more with it.  Great technical shot though.</td>', 'lighting is good, use of space is good, crop is good, subject (while attractive) leaves something to be desired.  it''s a little unnatural I guess ("hmm. there''s a maid.  and there''s her boob".)  They''re good boobs, don''t get me wrong, but I think you could have done more with it.  Great technical shot though.', '2003-07-11 19:27:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(354128, 27532, 6388, '<td valign="top">points for the title, but I''m struggling with the rest.  I understand the subtlety, it''s just not working for me.</td>', 'points for the title, but I''m struggling with the rest.  I understand the subtlety, it''s just not working for me.', '2003-07-11 19:29:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(354129, 28052, 6388, '<td valign="top">It''s a nicely lit, nicely composed, well focused  picture of a cat.  in a fur coat, as it were.  Composition/technicals are nice.  would have received an 8 from me if this were a cat challenge.</td>', 'It''s a nicely lit, nicely composed, well focused  picture of a cat.  in a fur coat, as it were.  Composition/technicals are nice.  would have received an 8 from me if this were a cat challenge.', '2003-07-11 19:31:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(354131, 28288, 7628, '<td valign="top">I like the tone of the skin, and the way the light sculpts her muscles.  Wish her hand weren''t cropped.  While the rumpled white quilt makes a very nice background the buttons are a bit distracting.</td>', 'I like the tone of the skin, and the way the light sculpts her muscles.  Wish her hand weren''t cropped.  While the rumpled white quilt makes a very nice background the buttons are a bit distracting.', '2003-07-11 19:34:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(354132, 28287, 6388, '<td valign="top">if the challenge were ''almost nude'' or ''bikini'' or just about anything other than ''nude''  I''d have given this a 7 (for creativity, colour/desturation, lighting, composition etc).  At least it''s not just a picture of a toe. :)</td>', 'if the challenge were ''almost nude'' or ''bikini'' or just about anything other than ''nude''  I''d have given this a 7 (for creativity, colour/desturation, lighting, composition etc).  At least it''s not just a picture of a toe. :)', '2003-07-11 19:34:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(354134, 28248, 4007, '<td valign="top">I like the pose and lighting here.  It seems like an effective composition as a whole.  I really like the abstract shape it produces if you let your eyes release their focus a little bit.  I do take issue with the inclusion of both the b&amp;w and color versions.  I can see why you''d want to include both, as they each have different strengths and weaknesses.  I think I prefer the black and white version, because it emphasizes the forms better, seems to have a smoother flow to it, and I much prefer the shadowed black hair to the brown of the color.  The color version has more warmth to it and seems more personal than the cold b&amp;w shot.  So while I think both of these individually are good shots, I think the combination of the two results in a clash.  The color and black and white doesn''t flow together into one seemless shot.  Instead of bringing out each others advantages they seem to dull each other''s strengths.  So, I like the reflection (which I''m guessing was post-production produced and not an actual reflection) because of the added abstract quality it creates, but I''d have made the entire image black and white or color (and personal I''d have gone b&amp;w).  Great work though.  This might show up on my favorites. 9<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-07-18 00:47:06.</i></td>', 'I like the pose and lighting here.  It seems like an effective composition as a whole.  I really like the abstract shape it produces if you let your eyes release their focus a little bit.  I do take issue with the inclusion of both the b&w and color versions.  I can see why you''d want to include both, as they each have different strengths and weaknesses.  I think I prefer the black and white version, because it emphasizes the forms better, seems to have a smoother flow to it, and I much prefer the shadowed black hair to the brown of the color.  The color version has more warmth to it and seems more personal than the cold b&w shot.  So while I think both of these individually are good shots, I think the combination of the two results in a clash.  The color and black and white doesn''t flow together into one seemless shot.  Instead of bringing out each others advantages they seem to dull each other''s strengths.  So, I like the reflection (which I''m guessing was post-production produced and not an actual reflection) because of the added abstract quality it creates, but I''d have made the entire image black and white or color (and personal I''d have gone b&w).  Great work though.  This might show up on my favorites. 9', '2003-07-11 19:36:38.000000', '2003-07-18 01:47:06.000000', 1),
(354135, 28274, 7628, '<td valign="top">I love this idea - the shaddows of the blinds gently accentuate her curves, The rest of the light sculpts her body very nicely.  A nice cool comfortable feeling. I would like to see how it looks with the full curve of the bottom, and a bit of a crop on the top.</td>', 'I love this idea - the shaddows of the blinds gently accentuate her curves, The rest of the light sculpts her body very nicely.  A nice cool comfortable feeling. I would like to see how it looks with the full curve of the bottom, and a bit of a crop on the top.', '2003-07-11 19:38:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(354155, 28283, 7994, '<td valign="top">great photo, i think color would add on impression it makes</td>', 'great photo, i think color would add on impression it makes', '2003-07-11 19:53:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(354156, 28248, 1779, '<td valign="top">I was expecting so much more from this chllenge...  fortunately your work is one of the better ones. The idea is simple but elegant.  I would´ve give the B&amp;W a bit more contrast and desaturated the color one. never the less good job!<br/> <br/>LM</td>', 'I was expecting so much more from this chllenge...  fortunately your work is one of the better ones. The idea is simple but elegant.  I would´ve give the B&W a bit more contrast and desaturated the color one. never the less good job! LM', '2003-07-11 19:55:01.000000', NULL, 1),
