(354298, 28191, 772, '<td valign="top">I hate it when this situation comes up for me... To me, this is what i would call ''digital art'' moreso than photography.  Normally, I don''t care much for digital art, but it''s probably because I''m simply more of a ''purist'' photographer.  I have always been one who looks for the photographic quality and themes when judging an image on this site.  I must say that this is one of the first images I have seen that really falls into the digital art category for me that I''m really impressed by overall.  I''m assuming that this is a composite image simply because I don''t see (easily) any other way to do it.  What I also see here is some very creative use/combination of photography and digital art to create your ''vision'' for this piece.  I''m impressed and moved by this image at the same time.  Kudos on some good work :) = 10</td>', 'I hate it when this situation comes up for me... To me, this is what i would call ''digital art'' moreso than photography.  Normally, I don''t care much for digital art, but it''s probably because I''m simply more of a ''purist'' photographer.  I have always been one who looks for the photographic quality and themes when judging an image on this site.  I must say that this is one of the first images I have seen that really falls into the digital art category for me that I''m really impressed by overall.  I''m assuming that this is a composite image simply because I don''t see (easily) any other way to do it.  What I also see here is some very creative use/combination of photography and digital art to create your ''vision'' for this piece.  I''m impressed and moved by this image at the same time.  Kudos on some good work :) = 10', '2003-07-11 22:52:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(354300, 28281, 472, '<td valign="top">i really like the model the pose the title and the idea but i would like to recommend that you shoot this pic with different lighting than the oncamera flash. in general,  that kind of lighting just illuminates very directly, without any sparkle or mystery.  try a lamp from like a 45 degree angle to the subject.</td>', 'i really like the model the pose the title and the idea but i would like to recommend that you shoot this pic with different lighting than the oncamera flash. in general,  that kind of lighting just illuminates very directly, without any sparkle or mystery.  try a lamp from like a 45 degree angle to the subject.', '2003-07-11 22:58:43.000000', NULL, 1),
