(354642, 28074, 806, '<td valign="top">nicely done! good job!<br/> <br/><b>edit</b>:<br/> <br/>This image gives me the feeling of innocence - not just of a child, but of a free spirit. The shadow and use of sun for light is at the perfect angle, and the composition repeats that. Great leading lines with the footprints taking the eye from the lower left corner to the child at the upper right corner.  The perspective used (angle of camera to subject) is perfect to give just the right negative space.<br/>You don''t need to see this child''s face. She represents all people.<br/>I love this image. Congrats!</td>', 'nicely done! good job! edit: This image gives me the feeling of innocence - not just of a child, but of a free spirit. The shadow and use of sun for light is at the perfect angle, and the composition repeats that. Great leading lines with the footprints taking the eye from the lower left corner to the child at the upper right corner.  The perspective used (angle of camera to subject) is perfect to give just the right negative space.You don''t need to see this child''s face. She represents all people.I love this image. Congrats!', '2003-07-12 14:37:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(354649, 28005, 806, '<td valign="top">what an interesting shot! the white on white is done nicely to show smoothness of the skin.. untouched and "eve-like". The use of the hat is nice, however, I am not sure I like the style of the hat for this image. That said... the inference of touching the brim of the hat shows the story in motion. If you had instructed the model to actually hold the brim of the hat, it would have been the end of the story with nothing left to tell. nice work!<br/></td>', 'what an interesting shot! the white on white is done nicely to show smoothness of the skin.. untouched and "eve-like". The use of the hat is nice, however, I am not sure I like the style of the hat for this image. That said... the inference of touching the brim of the hat shows the story in motion. If you had instructed the model to actually hold the brim of the hat, it would have been the end of the story with nothing left to tell. nice work!', '2003-07-12 14:42:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(354665, 27790, 806, '<td valign="top">An image that speaks volumnes. It leaves me wondering what has happened to her. Neat how this follows along with "Unanswered Questions" as well as "Nude", as well as past challenges. If you have been at DPC for a while, this image shows everything you have learned. If you are an experienced photographer, new to the site or not, it still shows you have wrapped up all your knowledge in this shot.<br/>Negative space is done well.. The use of shapes besides the figure... The drama and emotion so often non-existent in photographs.... the lighting... <br/>congrats!<br/></td>', 'An image that speaks volumnes. It leaves me wondering what has happened to her. Neat how this follows along with "Unanswered Questions" as well as "Nude", as well as past challenges. If you have been at DPC for a while, this image shows everything you have learned. If you are an experienced photographer, new to the site or not, it still shows you have wrapped up all your knowledge in this shot.Negative space is done well.. The use of shapes besides the figure... The drama and emotion so often non-existent in photographs.... the lighting... congrats!', '2003-07-12 14:50:28.000000', NULL, 1),
