(360450, 28274, 6937, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the wonderfull feedback. In retrospect I probably should have re positioned the right arm out of the picture. Please keep in mind that this was a 500 watt Home Depot special through some throw away blinds not a $5,000 dollar light kit and studio. It was also taken with my old camera and not my new Canon d10. But thats why I like this site I learn from your comments and strive to be as good as some of you.<br/> <br/>Although If I had repositioned the right arm it would change the shape of the right breast in a not so positive way. Oh well cant take it back now.<br/> <br/>Again thanks for the comments.<br/> <br/>Kerry<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-07-18 00:36:39.</i></td>', 'Thanks for the wonderfull feedback. In retrospect I probably should have re positioned the right arm out of the picture. Please keep in mind that this was a 500 watt Home Depot special through some throw away blinds not a $5,000 dollar light kit and studio. It was also taken with my old camera and not my new Canon d10. But thats why I like this site I learn from your comments and strive to be as good as some of you. Although If I had repositioned the right arm it would change the shape of the right breast in a not so positive way. Oh well cant take it back now. Again thanks for the comments. Kerry', '2003-07-18 01:36:13.000000', '2003-07-18 01:36:39.000000', 0),
