(360742, 28005, 4564, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyobody!  I appreciate the positive feedback. The ribbon feels good too, I have to admit!  <br/> <br/>In response to magnetic9999''s question regarding compromise and photography, I didn''t compromise in this B&amp;W photo.  I understand it looks a lot softer than my previous entries on DPC, and it is, but traditional B&amp;W nude photography is also part of what I like to explore in photography.  After the "controversial" COVER photo I submitted (yellow tiny bikini), I wanted to show that it was also possible to shoot a conventional and classic photo with the same not so conventional but still very classy and lovely model.  The NUDE challenge was probably the best challenge I could use to show that because I wouldn''t be penalized for the skin factor.  The photo being of a softer nature also helped.<br/> <br/>With my submissions on DPC, I''ll have to admit I like to stir up discussions.  I think awareness, curiosity and being open minded are key elements to a good photographer.  In this field of work, you learn all the time, all your life.  Even though you may specialize in a specific theme, or to the contrary, may avoid exploring specific photography themes for x reason, as a photographer it is important to stay open to others in order to learn.  Conventions must fall in order to stay open.  It doesn''t mean we need to like and support everything.  But by being aware and receptive, we allow ourselves the great opporunity to learn from one another.  DPC is a special place because it gives photographers the unique chance to meet with one another and share.  Even though it is done in a virtual world, the basis of being able to exchange ideas, share our work, and take part in dicussions with other like-minded photographers is very important for artists.  It allow us to evolve and surpass ourselves in our art.  It also allow us to question ourselves.  And in the end, hopefully, it allow us to also evolve as a person.<br/> <br/> <br/>I thank you for comments.  <br/>Enjoy photography, it is a great art.<br/> <br/>Martin<br/>aka. DrJones<br/> <br/></td>', 'Thanks everyobody!  I appreciate the positive feedback. The ribbon feels good too, I have to admit!   In response to magnetic9999''s question regarding compromise and photography, I didn''t compromise in this B&W photo.  I understand it looks a lot softer than my previous entries on DPC, and it is, but traditional B&W nude photography is also part of what I like to explore in photography.  After the "controversial" COVER photo I submitted (yellow tiny bikini), I wanted to show that it was also possible to shoot a conventional and classic photo with the same not so conventional but still very classy and lovely model.  The NUDE challenge was probably the best challenge I could use to show that because I wouldn''t be penalized for the skin factor.  The photo being of a softer nature also helped. With my submissions on DPC, I''ll have to admit I like to stir up discussions.  I think awareness, curiosity and being open minded are key elements to a good photographer.  In this field of work, you learn all the time, all your life.  Even though you may specialize in a specific theme, or to the contrary, may avoid exploring specific photography themes for x reason, as a photographer it is important to stay open to others in order to learn.  Conventions must fall in order to stay open.  It doesn''t mean we need to like and support everything.  But by being aware and receptive, we allow ourselves the great opporunity to learn from one another.  DPC is a special place because it gives photographers the unique chance to meet with one another and share.  Even though it is done in a virtual world, the basis of being able to exchange ideas, share our work, and take part in dicussions with other like-minded photographers is very important for artists.  It allow us to evolve and surpass ourselves in our art.  It also allow us to question ourselves.  And in the end, hopefully, it allow us to also evolve as a person.  I thank you for comments.  Enjoy photography, it is a great art. Martinaka. DrJones ', '2003-07-18 14:09:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(360746, 28005, 7711, '<td valign="top">Martin..this was a fabulous shot. I knew it was yours from the start and it was one of my two favourites of the challenge. Your story is a riot too...I wish I had 10% that much talent and skill. :) Congratulations on your first ribbon! It feels like justice for all the shots of yours that should have won.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-07-18 22:29:33.</i></td>', 'Martin..this was a fabulous shot. I knew it was yours from the start and it was one of my two favourites of the challenge. Your story is a riot too...I wish I had 10% that much talent and skill. :) Congratulations on your first ribbon! It feels like justice for all the shots of yours that should have won.', '2003-07-18 14:16:13.000000', '2003-07-18 23:29:33.000000', 0),
