(360781, 27974, 472, '<td valign="top">thanks all for voting on and liking my entry.  i had actually done a few shots that i was considering submitting that were more like figure studies.  but i still wanted to do something out of the ordinary, stunning, theatrical, that left it open to the viewer to the interpret or a read a story into. <br/> <br/>that''s how i came up with the shot i submitted.  i had a number of ideas for titles, but whatever it was had to capture the ''fantasy'' quality of the image.  my favorite alternate title took into account the chair and was called ''executive muse''. <br/> <br/>my other <a href="//www.pbase.com/magnetic9999/nude" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">outtakes are here (warning: bare breasts ahead)</a>, if you are interested.  i am very interested to hear what people would have thought of them and if any of them would have been preferred.  personally, i very much liked the shots ''sea nymph'' and ''composure''.  <br/> <br/>Which are your favorites?</td>', 'thanks all for voting on and liking my entry.  i had actually done a few shots that i was considering submitting that were more like figure studies.  but i still wanted to do something out of the ordinary, stunning, theatrical, that left it open to the viewer to the interpret or a read a story into.  that''s how i came up with the shot i submitted.  i had a number of ideas for titles, but whatever it was had to capture the ''fantasy'' quality of the image.  my favorite alternate title took into account the chair and was called ''executive muse''.  my other outtakes are here (warning: bare breasts ahead), if you are interested.  i am very interested to hear what people would have thought of them and if any of them would have been preferred.  personally, i very much liked the shots ''sea nymph'' and ''composure''.   Which are your favorites?', '2003-07-18 15:15:39.000000', NULL, 0),
