(362993, 28017, 200, '<td valign="top">pedro...I think the softness is grain from playing with levels. The image was actually underexposed. Also...my images look soft after compression and uploading to this site...i need to figure a way around such things. Not many people approve of his pose...perhaps i should title this one..."breaking the rules". Why must I conform to preconcieved notions of right and wrong poses? To me, it works for him. Journey put it together quite nicely...thank you journey :)</td>', 'pedro...I think the softness is grain from playing with levels. The image was actually underexposed. Also...my images look soft after compression and uploading to this site...i need to figure a way around such things. Not many people approve of his pose...perhaps i should title this one..."breaking the rules". Why must I conform to preconcieved notions of right and wrong poses? To me, it works for him. Journey put it together quite nicely...thank you journey :)', '2003-07-21 23:10:27.000000', NULL, 0),
